From 7c05b5888769ddb84859c11a7fc49458eba7f67e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vili Kohonen <vili.kohonen@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:50:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Let a system prompt be a job parameter rather than a source
 edit

Every arm that conditions on a new prompt needed a patch to src/prompts.py, an image
rebuild, and a place in the patch chain -- for what is a string. Worse, the text then
lived in git rather than beside the run that used it, so reading a result meant finding
the commit the pod was on.

SYSTEM_PROMPTS now also merges {name: text} from the JSON file named by
RLRH_EXTRA_PROMPTS, if that variable is set. tools/rlrh_job.py writes that file from the
job parameters, which means the prompt text is hashed into the job id and stored with the
run instead of being inferred from a tag.

Existing keys cannot be overridden and a missing file is an error rather than a fallback:
both failure modes would produce a run that looks like the arm that was asked for and is
not. Appended at EOF so it composes with rh-anti-hack-prompts and rh-recontextualization
in any order.
---
 src/prompts.py | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/prompts.py b/src/prompts.py
index a3ba9fb..7bf2762 100644
--- a/src/prompts.py
+++ b/src/prompts.py
@@ -59,3 +59,46 @@ Please evaluate the following prompt and assistant response:
 """
 
 
+
+"""RUNTIME PROMPTS
+
+A system prompt is data, not code. Every prompt above had to be a source edit, which meant a
+patch and an image rebuild for each new idea about what to condition on -- and it meant the
+text of a run's prompt lived in git rather than beside the run.
+
+If RLRH_EXTRA_PROMPTS names a readable JSON file of {name: text}, those entries are merged in
+here and are then selectable by --prompt_name / --target_prompt_name like any other. Nothing
+else changes: the entrypoints still reject a name that does not resolve, so a typo is still an
+error rather than a silently empty system prompt.
+
+Two things this deliberately does not do. It does not override an existing key -- the published
+prompts are quotations and a run claiming `dont_eval_game` must have used that text. And it adds
+nothing to the prompt: whatever the file says is the whole system prompt, minus the format suffix
+the entrypoints append, so a prompt that wants the neutral lead-in has to carry it.
+
+Appended at the end of the file on purpose, so this patch composes with any other patch to
+src/prompts.py in either order.
+"""
+
+import json as _json
+import os as _os
+
+_extra_path = _os.environ.get("RLRH_EXTRA_PROMPTS")
+if _extra_path:
+    if not _os.path.isfile(_extra_path):
+        raise FileNotFoundError(
+            f"RLRH_EXTRA_PROMPTS={_extra_path} does not exist. Refusing to fall back to the "
+            f"built-in prompts: the run would look like the arm that was asked for and would "
+            f"be a different one."
+        )
+    with open(_extra_path) as _f:
+        for _name, _text in _json.load(_f).items():
+            if _name in SYSTEM_PROMPTS:
+                raise ValueError(
+                    f"RLRH_EXTRA_PROMPTS redefines {_name!r}, which is a published prompt. "
+                    f"Pick another name."
+                )
+            if not isinstance(_text, str) or not _text.strip():
+                raise ValueError(f"RLRH_EXTRA_PROMPTS entry {_name!r} is not a non-empty string")
+            SYSTEM_PROMPTS[_name] = _text
+    print(f"Loaded {len(SYSTEM_PROMPTS)} system prompts, including from {_extra_path}")
-- 
